{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the earth, and behold it was corrupted.</b> This is idolatry, for He sees none but HaShem alone, since the root of heresy is in the heart. And for this reason it is stated concerning idolatry (Ezekiel 14:5) ״לְמַעַן תְּפֹשׂ אֶת בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּלִבָּם״, for the essence of faith is in the heart. ״כִּי הִשְׁחִית כָּל בָּשָׂר אֶת דַּרְכּוֹ״ — this is forbidden sexual relations, which is called ״דַּרְכּוֹ״, as in ״דֶרֶךְ גֶּבֶר בְּעַלְמָה״ (Proverbs 30:19). And according to our Rabbis of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 26:4) they sinned through the wasteful emission of seed; therefore it says ״עַל הָאָרֶץ״, as it says (Genesis 38:9) ״וְשִׁחֵת אָרְצָה״. And this will be explained further nearby, regarding the description of righteous and blameless, in the verse ״כִּי אוֹתְךָ רָאִיתִי צַדִּיק לְפָנַי״. And as for what is stated, ״וְהִנְנִי מַשְׁחִיתָם אֶת הָאָרֶץ״ — that even the earth became corrupted — this will be explained, with the help of HaShem, in the portion of אַחֲרֵי מוֹת (Leviticus 18:25) in the verse ״וַתִּטְמָא הָאָרֶץ וָאֶפְקֹד עֲוֹנָהּ עָלֶיהָ״, that the earth is touched by the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:22.029963496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}